  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Department of Veterans Affairs contract obligations total $51.8B in FY2026 to date. The agency has made 56,431 awards so far, with an average award size of $919K. Obligations fell 33.8% year over year. These totals are partial, fiscal year to date, and represent contract obligations only. Looking back, obligations rose from $47.7B in FY21 to $78.3B in FY25 before the FY2026 to date total of $51.8B. Spending in FY2026 to date is concentrated in health and medical categories and in a handful of large vendors that account for multi-billion dollar shares of the total. That concentration helps explain the large average award size and the marked year-over-year drop when some big contracts did not carry over into the current fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 33.8% year over year. That decline follows a peak of $78.3B in FY25 and a FY2026 to date total of $51.8B. The drop is notable given the prior multi-year increase from $47.7B in FY21 to $78.3B in FY25. Large, uneven vendor and category spend creates volatility between fiscal years."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where is the money going by category and vendor?",
        "body": "The largest category is Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers at $14.4B, followed by Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing at $9.9B and Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) at $7.6B. On the vendor side, MCKESSON CORPORATION leads with $9.6B, TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP is next with $7.9B, and OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. accounts for $6.6B. Together a few categories and vendors represent a large share of the FY2026 to date obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Veterans Affairs spend on contracts?",
      "a": "They have $51.8B in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The agency has made 56,431 awards, with an average award size of $919K. These totals are partial, fiscal year to date, and obligations fell 33.8% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Veterans Affairs buy?",
      "a": "Mostly health and medical services and products. The top category is Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers at $14.4B, followed by Pharmaceutical Preparation Manufacturing at $9.9B and Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) at $7.6B. Other sizable categories include Computer Systems Design Services at $3.1B and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $2.1B."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Veterans Affairs's largest contractors?",
      "a": "MCKESSON CORPORATION, TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP, and OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. are the largest by obligations. MCKESSON CORPORATION has $9.6B, TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP has $7.9B, and OPTUM PUBLIC SECTOR SOLUTIONS, INC. has $6.6B. Other top vendors include QTC MEDICAL SERVICES INC at $2.2B, OPTUMSERVE HEALTH SERVICES, INC. at $1.8B, and LOYAL SOURCE GOVERNMENT SERVICES LLC at $1.8B."
